{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויחדלו", :translit "va'yechdelu", :gloss "and they ceased"} {:he "ויחדלו הקולות", :translit "va'yechdelu ha'kolot", :gloss "and the sounds ceased"} {:he "ויחדלו לבנות העיר", :translit "va'yechdelu livnot ha'ir", :gloss "and they ceased building the city"} {:he "בדור הפלגה", :translit "b'dor ha'palagah", :gloss "in the generation of the dispersion"} {:he "קולות", :translit "kolot", :gloss "sounds"} {:he "וערבבם עד שחדלו לבנות", :translit "ve'aravam ad she'chadelu livnot", :gloss "and mixed them up until they ceased building"} {:he "חדלו לבנות ע\"י הקולות שיצאו מתחת סבלות מצרים", :translit "chadelu livnot al yedei ha'kolot she'yatz'u mitachat sivlot mitzrayim", :gloss "they ceased building by means of the sounds that went out from under the burdens of Egypt"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ויחדלו הקולות" "ויחדלו לבנות העיר"]}], :frame {:text "The generation of the Dispersion (dor ha-palagah) built the Tower of Babel, and God confounded their language so they could not understand one another's speech (Genesis 11:7–8). The Midrash describes that God dispersed them by means of various sounds that confused them (Tanchuma, Noach 19; Bereshit Rabbah 38:6). The Ba'al HaTurim reads the rare word ויחדלו as a linguistic bridge between these two events: just as sounds caused the builders of Babel to cease building (Genesis 11:8), so too the sounds of the plague of hail ceased at Moses' prayer.", :sources ["Genesis 11:7–8" "Bereshit Rabbah 38:6" "Tanchuma Noach 19"]}} {:quotes [{:he "נתך", :translit "natokh", :gloss "he poured"} {:he "לא נתך ארצה", :translit "lo natokh artzah", :gloss "it did not pour [upon the] earth"} {:he "עד נתך מים עליהם", :translit "ad natokh mayim aleihem", :gloss "until he poured water upon them"} {:he "בני שאול המוקעים", :translit "b'nei sha'ul ha'mukaim", :gloss "the sons of Saul who were impaled"} {:he "כאשר נתך אפי וחמתי על יושבי ירושלים", :translit "ka'asher natokh api ve'chamati al yoshvei yerushalayim", :gloss "as I poured my anger and wrath upon the inhabitants of Jerusalem"} {:he "תפלת הצדיקים", :translit "tefilat ha'tzadikim", :gloss "prayer of the righteous"} {:he "וכפר אדמתו עמו", :translit "ve'khiper admato amo", :gloss "and he will atone his land his people"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["לא נתך ארצה" "עד נתך מים עליהם" "כאשר נתך אפי וחמתי על יושבי ירושלים"]}], :frame {:text "The second occurrence of the root נתך appears in the narrative of David and the Gibeonites: David hands over seven descendants of Saul to be impaled, and after that the verse states 'And they buried them… and afterward God was entreated for the land' (2 Samuel 21:14), which the Talmud reads as David praying for rain that fell and atoned for the land (Yevamot 78b). The third occurrence comes in God's declaration 'as I poured out My anger and wrath upon the inhabitants of Jerusalem' (Ezekiel 22:31), a passage understood as Jerusalem suffering for its sins but destined for atonement. Deuteronomy 32:43 states 'and He will atone His land and His people,' a verse interpreted as atonement coming to the land through Israel's prayers (Sifrei Ha'azinu 335). The Ba'al HaTurim links these three נתך verses to show that the righteous can both withhold rain, as Moses withheld the hail, and bring it down, as David brought rain after the executions.", :sources ["2 Samuel 21:1–14" "Yevamot 78b" "Ezekiel 22:31" "Deuteronomy 32:43" "Sifrei Ha'azinu 335"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ויחדלו הקולות" "ויחדלו לבנות העיר"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ויחדלו הקולות", :refs ["Exodus 9:33"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "ויחדלו לבנות העיר", :refs ["Genesis 11:8"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["לא נתך ארצה" "עד נתך מים עליהם" "כאשר נתך אפי וחמתי על יושבי ירושלים"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "לא נתך ארצה", :refs ["Exodus 9:33"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "עד נתך מים עליהם", :refs ["2 Samuel 21:10"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "כאשר נתך אפי וחמתי על יושבי ירושלים", :refs ["Jeremiah 42:18"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive}]}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:14:51.603915127Z", :model "glm-5.2"}